<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Madinat al-Zahira</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">979–1009</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Madinat al-Zahira was the palace and administrative city built by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almanzor">Almanzor</a> from about 979 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>, to which he moved the offices of government, leaving the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hisham-ii">Hisham II</a> isolated in his palace. It was the seat of the Amirid regime until 1009, when it was sacked and destroyed in the revolt that began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fitna-of-al-andalus">Fitna of al-Andalus</a>. Its exact site has not been identified.</p></div>
